{"slug":"05_sim_and_sensor_realism","cells":[{"kind":"markdown","src":"# 05 — Simulation World and Sensor Realism\n\nspecter-1's sim is 2D, deterministic, and **noisy on purpose**. ADR 0005 records the sensor-realism budget — every channel has a noise model that survives the port to ROS2/Gazebo:\n\n* **Lidar** — `P_DROP = 2%` returns are `math.inf`; range-dependent σ ramps linearly with distance.\n* **IMU** — per-agent bias drift (initial σ=0.01, random-walk σ=0.0005/tick).\n* **UWB beacons** — DWM1000-class noise (`σ_beacon_range = 0.10 m`), 5° PDOA bearing, 2% NLOS multipath (`σ_NLOS = 0.07 m`).\n\n**UWB beacons are load-bearing.** As of ADR 0015 (Range-Only Trust Voting), `range_m` and `bearing_rad` from the UWB channel are **the only scalars the trust engine consumes**. Lidar drives SLAM (which never enters the trust path); IMU drives gyro (also SLAM-only). The trust layer reads beacon returns and nothing else. A hardware port that fakes lidar but ships real UWB still produces correct trust output."},{"kind":"code","src":"%matplotlib inline\nimport os\nfrom pathlib import Path\n# Notebook runs from notebooks/; chdir to project root so scenarios/*.yaml resolve.\n_root = Path.cwd().parent if Path.cwd().name == 'notebooks' else Path.cwd()\nos.chdir(_root)\nfrom specter.demo import build_swarm, snapshot, step\nfrom specter.viz.notebook import world_figure","outputs":[]},{"kind":"markdown","src":"## Intuition: build a 2-agent world, advance one tick, render the frame\n\n`build_swarm` constructs the full hardened pipeline (sim + identities + roster + bus + evaluators + SLAM + mergers). For visualization purposes we only need the sim; the rest is dormant until we feed it attacks."},{"kind":"code","src":"state = build_swarm('scenarios/two_agents.yaml')\nfor _ in range(20):\n    step(state)\nsnap = snapshot(state)\nfig = world_figure(snap)","outputs":[{"kind":"image","mime":"image/png","b64":""}]},{"kind":"markdown","src":"## Intuition: lidar dropouts and range-dependent noise\n\nA lidar return at distance d has σ ∝ (1 + d/10) and a 2% chance of dropping. The histogram below shows how many beams returned vs. dropped over a 200-tick run."},{"kind":"code","src":"import math\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\nvalid = 0\ndropped = 0\nstate2 = build_swarm('scenarios/two_agents.yaml')\nfor _ in range(200):\n    tick = step(state2)\n    for agent_id, scans in tick.scans.items():\n        for m in scans:\n            if math.isinf(m.distance):\n                dropped += 1\n            else:\n                valid += 1\nrate = dropped / (valid + dropped)\nprint(f'valid: {valid}  dropped: {dropped}  rate: {rate:.3%}')\nfig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(5, 3))\nax.bar(['valid', 'dropped'], [valid, dropped], color=['#7a9b5e', '#d4583a'])\nax.set_title(f'lidar returns over 200 ticks (drop rate = {rate:.2%})')\nax.set_ylabel('beam count');","outputs":[{"kind":"text","text":"valid: 14129  dropped: 271  rate: 1.882%\n"},{"kind":"image","mime":"image/png","b64":""}]},{"kind":"markdown","src":"## Claim: the sensor budget is locked in ADR 0005 — UWB-range column promoted by ADR 0015\n\nThese constants are the contract a hardware port must match (or substitute with calibrated real-sensor data). The eval battery passes against this budget; if a TurtleBot4 lidar has a different drop pattern, the threshold tuning re-runs.\n\n| Channel | Constant | Used by trust engine? | Rationale |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Lidar `P_DROP` | 2% | No — SLAM only | Industry-typical for indoor environments |\n| Lidar σ ramp | 1 + d/10 | No — SLAM only | DWM-class spec |\n| IMU bias drift σ | 0.01 init / 0.0005 RW | No — gyro/SLAM only | Consumer-grade IMU spec |\n| **UWB `range_m`** | `σ_beacon_range = 0.10 m` | **Yes — Tier 1 + Tier 2** | DWM1000 datasheet |\n| **UWB NLOS** | 2% events, `σ_NLOS = 0.07 m` | **Yes — feeds `σ_combined`** | DWM1000 datasheet |\n| UWB `bearing_rad` | 5° PDOA | Used by sim for sybil geometry; trust engine does not consume bearing | PDOA limit |\n\nADR 0005 captures the rationale; ADR 0015 promotes the UWB range column from \"realism flavor\" to \"trust contract\". The `tests/eval/` battery validates the engine against this budget."},{"kind":"markdown","src":"## Limit\n\nThis is **simulated noise, not Gazebo PointCloud2**. The Phase-1 entry criterion in `docs/HARDWARE_READINESS.md` is exactly: \"battery passes over real DDS in Gazebo\". When that lands, this notebook gets a sibling running the same sensors against Gazebo replay logs. Until then, every claim above is conditional on the budget matching real hardware."}]}